# Dolby Pro Logic II Downmixer

Real-time 5.1 channel to Dolby Pro Logic II audio downmixer for Windows.

This application captures multi-channel (5.1) surround sound audio from Windows games or media players in real-time and encodes it into a Dolby Pro Logic II compatible matrix-encoded stereo signal using NAudio and WASAPI.

Required

To capture multi-channel audio in real-time, **VB-Audio Virtual Cable (or Virtual Audio Cable)** is **REQUIRED**.

1. Download and install [VB-Audio Cable](https://vb-audio.com/Cable/).
2. Set **CABLE Input** as your **Default Playback Device** in Windows Sound settings.
3. Configure **CABLE Input** speaker setup in Windows to **5.1 Surround**.
4. Run **AudioDownmixerGUI**, select **CABLE Output** as the input source, and choose your main stereo output device (AV Receiver, Soundbar, or Headphones).

---

## Features

* **Real-time 5.1 to DPL II Matrix Encoding:** Downmixes Surround L/R, Center, Subwoofer, and Rear Surround channels into standard stereo output.
* **Low Latency:** Uses WASAPI Loopback capture for minimal latency during gaming and media playback.
* **System Tray Integration:** Runs quietly in the background.
